{"questions":[{"question_id":"mnswhyfs","content":"<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"43.439ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 19200 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> Match List - I with List - II. </text></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<table class=\"tg\"><thead>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <th class=\"tg-baqh\" colspan=\"2\">List - I<br>Purification technique</th>\n\n    <th class=\"tg-baqh\" colspan=\"2\">List - II<br>Used to separate</th>\n\n  </tr></thead>\n\n<tbody>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">A.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Simple distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">I.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Steam volatile compound</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">B.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Fractional distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">II.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Two liquids with large difference in boiling points</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">C.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Steam distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">III.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Liquid decomposing at its boiling point</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">D.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Distillation under reduced pressure</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">IV.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Two liquids with close boiling points</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2026-online-5th-april-evening-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 5th April Evening Shift","permalink":"p-text--match-list-i-with-list-ii--p-style-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-ixl19aovbzk9evqc","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"43.439ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 19200 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> Match List - I with List - II. </text></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<table class=\"tg\"><thead>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <th class=\"tg-baqh\" colspan=\"2\">List - I<br>Purification technique</th>\n\n    <th class=\"tg-baqh\" colspan=\"2\">List - II<br>Used to separate</th>\n\n  </tr></thead>\n\n<tbody>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">A.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Simple distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">I.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Steam volatile compound</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">B.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Fractional distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">II.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Two liquids with large difference in boiling points</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">C.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Steam distillation</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">III.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Liquid decomposing at its boiling point</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n  <tr>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">D.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Distillation under reduced pressure</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">IV.</td>\n\n    <td class=\"tg-baqh\">Two liquids with close boiling points</td>\n\n  </tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I</p>"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<h3>A. Simple distillation</h3>\n<p>Simple distillation is used to separate <strong>two liquids with a large difference in boiling points</strong>.</p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.497ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 3313.6 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1027.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2305.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2809.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<h3>B. Fractional distillation</h3>\n<p>Fractional distillation is used to separate <strong>two liquids with close boiling points</strong>.</p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.117ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 3587.6 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1036.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2314.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2818.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<h3>C. Steam distillation</h3>\n<p>Steam distillation is used for separating a <strong>steam volatile compound</strong>.</p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.379ex\" height=\"1.645ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 2819.6 727\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1037.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2315.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<h3>D. Distillation under reduced pressure</h3>\n<p>This method is used for a <strong>liquid that decomposes at its boiling point</strong>. By reducing pressure, the boiling point decreases and decomposition is avoided.</p>\n<p>So,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.813ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 3895.6 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D437\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D437\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1105.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2383.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2887.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3391.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Thus, the correct matching is:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"34.882ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 15417.8 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(972.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1972.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2476.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2980.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></us